[{:db/id 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4bf3edf8-7469-5b33-bc3b-54f4acae6cf1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192510 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, x^2+y^2 \\geq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A - \\partial A = \\textrm{int}\\, A$\n\nII. $\\textrm{int}\\, A \\cap \\partial A = \\emptyset$\n\nIII. $A = \\textrm{int}\\,A \\cup \\partial A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278570 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y\\ge {x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0fc95ee69ce7121c0cf8ae68029b135d9667f50275227d141f1d979f85408859.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the  parabola $-2y={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y={x}^{2}\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186398555 :question/problem "![](images/11/112ab676fa5a97db198a872c33579900deab76e0c3c9c92016e165a67482bbcd.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/44/44f3a2a8e535c7248dac49d126da9bf17fce94c357f15c93a3eaad665e73b47a.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278568 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b1/b1074330fc650cf6af682f173f50943d779819afa59bf5be19edb88def1ef03a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bf3edf8-7469-5b33-bc3b-54f4acae6cf1" :question/id #uuid "4bf3edf8-7469-5b33-bc3b-54f4acae6cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161595" :question/problem "![](images/65/6559dfed58b9456d6eebfd660f7a0d59a60db9db1159561f010f6b7e13e90e5b.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d7/d7293d96b71f573dbdcbfb491646f0e563f8ad1567eab5baaf960533e72d473f.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2-x\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4437d06f-222c-582a-ab1b-38dd45632e8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4437d06f-222c-582a-ab1b-38dd45632e8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4437d06f-222c-582a-ab1b-38dd45632e8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12dc85bb-cd47-5b33-a127-8e0086b71833" "answer-db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" "answer-4abb66be-2678-58be-a9b9-2a2311d4b784" "answer-6dc57868-eec7-5486-9156-13dad63ee061" "answer-4f38e133-dcd8-5339-a2b7-5a9997c0d1f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12dc85bb-cd47-5b33-a127-8e0086b71833" :answer/id #uuid "12dc85bb-cd47-5b33-a127-8e0086b71833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" :answer/id #uuid "db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4abb66be-2678-58be-a9b9-2a2311d4b784" :answer/id #uuid "4abb66be-2678-58be-a9b9-2a2311d4b784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dc57868-eec7-5486-9156-13dad63ee061" :answer/id #uuid "6dc57868-eec7-5486-9156-13dad63ee061" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\ge 2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f38e133-dcd8-5339-a2b7-5a9997c0d1f0" :answer/id #uuid "4f38e133-dcd8-5339-a2b7-5a9997c0d1f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\le 2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186398548 :question/problem "![](images/2b/2bb25857047d7a0200d4c58ee3756b0efa0f2d13aaca8664b1fe49414c18a461.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339008 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0\\le y<2\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/f4/f4ee8fbf9a7670a7d0e0b7488bccbf014f8db8fff0154c7db025f2b071aec566.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fc733f6966b016c93b6ee6a305c5af5ee4fa432dad5d95e28061fd2a0d33efb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281302 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<x<1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d6/d60700d57ddc72bb410b3136f546705676f83d23d9071ffe972c5163d11af549.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/75/75e0132cd3854f18e9ab409b7fd13af3898f78b5174647bf2b33b8438b9228cb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401268 :question/problem "![](images/af/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c030c9fae58742cb10f74.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/3d/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281311 :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278574 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193207 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378850 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378871 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$\n\nII. $A⊂\\text{int}A$\n\nIII. $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192917 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
